    "category": "COLOR SPACES",
    "highlighterClass": "highlight-purple",
    "title": "RGB \u2192 YCbCr and Chroma Subsampling",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-3014\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><rect x=\"14.0\" y=\"22.0\" width=\"44.0\" height=\"32.0\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"36.0\" y=\"19\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">frame</text><text x=\"36\" y=\"42\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">R G B</text><line x1=\"60.0\" y1=\"38.0\" x2=\"82.0\" y2=\"38.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-3014)\"/><rect x=\"82\" y=\"22\" width=\"40\" height=\"32\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"102\" y=\"36\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">3\u00d73</text><text x=\"102\" y=\"46\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">matrix</text><line x1=\"122.0\" y1=\"38.0\" x2=\"140.0\" y2=\"38.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-3014)\"/><rect x=\"140.0\" y=\"14.0\" width=\"40.0\" height=\"32.0\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#d9dee7\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"160\" y=\"33\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">Y</text><rect x=\"190.0\" y=\"14.0\" width=\"20.0\" height=\"16.0\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"25\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">Cb</text><rect x=\"190.0\" y=\"34.0\" width=\"20.0\" height=\"16.0\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"45\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">Cr</text><text x=\"160\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">full size</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">half size</text><line x1=\"14\" y1=\"80\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"80\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.6\" stroke-dasharray=\"1 3\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"96\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">Y = 0.299 R + 0.587 G + 0.114 B</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"108\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">Cb = \u22120.169 R \u2212 0.331 G + 0.5 B</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"120\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">Cr = 0.5 R \u2212 0.419 G \u2212 0.081 B</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"136\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">keep every Y pixel, share the colour (4:2:0)</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "The R, G, B frame goes through a 3\u00d73 matrix to a full-size Y plane and two half-size colour planes Cb, Cr (4:2:0).",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>What:</strong> YCbCr separates brightness <strong>Y</strong> from two color-difference signals <strong>Cb</strong> (blue minus luma) and <strong>Cr</strong> (red minus luma).",
      "<strong>How:</strong> A fixed 3\u00d73 matrix (Rec. 601 weights 0.299, 0.587, 0.114 for R, G, B) turns RGB into Y, Cb, Cr, with +128 added to Cb and Cr for 8-bit storage.",
      "<strong>Why:</strong> Human vision resolves luminance detail much better than color detail, so JPEG/video halve or quarter the chroma planes (4:2:2, 4:2:0) with little visible loss."
    ],
    "math": "$$\\begin{pmatrix}Y\\\\C_b\\\\C_r\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}0.299&0.587&0.114\\\\-0.1687&-0.3313&0.5\\\\0.5&-0.4187&-0.0813\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}R\\\\G\\\\B\\end{pmatrix}$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Fitting more street on the recorder.</strong> The camera's recorder stores the black-and-white picture at full detail and the two colour pictures at half size. The shop sign stays crisp; only the colour fringes on its edges are coarser.",
    "examTrap": "Subsampling is applied to Cb and Cr only, never to Y. Also Y in Rec. 601 weights green most (0.587), not (R+G+B)/3.",
    "stmtKind": "ALGORITHM",
    "statement": "<b>RGB to YCbCr (ITU-R BT.601) and chroma subsampling.</b> $\\begin{pmatrix}Y\\\\C_b\\\\C_r\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}0.299&0.587&0.114\\\\-0.1687&-0.3313&0.5\\\\0.5&-0.4187&-0.0813\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}R\\\\G\\\\B\\end{pmatrix}$, with $128$ added to $C_b,C_r$ for 8-bit storage. In 4:2:0 subsampling $Y$ is kept at full resolution while $C_b$ and $C_r$ are each stored at half resolution in both directions.",
    "hint": "Which part of the street frame must stay sharp, and which part can be stored at half size without anyone noticing?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$Y$ row $(0.299,0.587,0.114)$ = the brightness picture.</strong> Green is weighted most because the eye finds it brightest; this plane alone is the black-and-white frame.",
      "<strong>$C_b,C_r$ rows = blue-minus-brightness and red-minus-brightness.</strong> Each row sums to zero, so a grey pixel gives $C_b=C_r=0$ (128 after the offset).",
      "<strong>Half-size $C_b,C_r$ = the saving.</strong> The eye sees fine detail in brightness but not in colour, so the recorder keeps every $Y$ pixel and shares each colour sample among four."
    ],
