    "title": "HSI / HSV: Hue, Saturation, Intensity",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-3015\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><circle cx=\"70.0\" cy=\"76.0\" r=\"48.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><circle cx=\"70.0\" cy=\"76.0\" r=\"3.0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"70.0\" y1=\"76.0\" x2=\"70.0\" y2=\"28.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.6\" stroke-dasharray=\"1 3\"/><text x=\"64.0\" y=\"25.0\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">R 0\u00b0</text><line x1=\"70.0\" y1=\"76.0\" x2=\"111.6\" y2=\"100.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.6\" stroke-dasharray=\"1 3\"/><text x=\"117.6\" y=\"108.0\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">G 120\u00b0</text><line x1=\"70.0\" y1=\"76.0\" x2=\"28.4\" y2=\"100.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.6\" stroke-dasharray=\"1 3\"/><text x=\"25.84\" y=\"108.0\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">B 240\u00b0</text><line x1=\"70.0\" y1=\"76.0\" x2=\"98.0\" y2=\"56.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-3015)\"/><circle cx=\"98.0\" cy=\"56.0\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"102\" y=\"54\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">colour</text><path d=\"M88,76 A18,18 0 0 0 85.5,67\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/><text x=\"90\" y=\"80\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">H</text><text x=\"68\" y=\"86\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">S = radius</text><rect x=\"138\" y=\"20\" width=\"90\" height=\"24\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"183\" y=\"36\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">I = (R+G+B)/3</text><rect x=\"138\" y=\"52\" width=\"90\" height=\"24\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"183\" y=\"68\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">S = 1 \u2212 3\u00b7min/(R+G+B)</text><rect x=\"138\" y=\"84\" width=\"90\" height=\"24\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"183\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">H = angle \u03b8 (or 360\u00b0 \u2212 \u03b8)</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"136\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">grey \u21d2 S = 0 \u21d2 hue undefined</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "A colour on the wheel: the arrow's angle is the hue H and its length is the saturation S; I = (R+G+B)/3 is the brightness. Grey has S = 0, so its hue is undefined.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Hue $H$</strong> is the angle on the color wheel (which pure color), <strong>Saturation $S$</strong> is how far from gray (how pure), <strong>Intensity $I$</strong> is how bright.",
      "The formulas: $I=\\frac{R+G+B}{3}$, $S = 1-\\frac{3\\min(R,G,B)}{R+G+B}$, and $H$ comes from the angle $\\theta=\\cos^{-1}\\!\\big(\\frac{\\tfrac12[(R-G)+(R-B)]}{\\sqrt{(R-G)^2+(R-B)(G-B)}}\\big)$.",
      "It matches how people name colors, so you can <strong>change brightness without shifting hue</strong>, handy for equalizing only I."
    ],
    "math": "$$I=\\frac{R+G+B}{3},\\quad S=1-\\frac{3\\min(R,G,B)}{R+G+B},\\quad H=\\begin{cases}\\theta & B\\le G\\\\ 360^\\circ-\\theta & B>G\\end{cases}$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Brighten the night frame, keep the bus red.</strong> Work on $I$ alone: the dim bus gets brighter and stays the same red, because hue and saturation are not touched.",
    "examTrap": "When S = 0 (gray, R=G=B) the hue is UNDEFINED, and when I = 0 saturation is undefined. Do not treat H = 0 as red in these cases.",
    "stmtKind": "DEFINITION",
    "statement": "<b>HSI colour model.</b> For $R,G,B\\in[0,1]$: $I=\\frac{R+G+B}{3}$, $S=1-\\frac{3\\min(R,G,B)}{R+G+B}$, and $H=\\theta$ if $B\\le G$, $H=360^\\circ-\\theta$ if $B\\gt G$, where $\\theta=\\cos^{-1}\\!\\Big(\\frac{\\frac12[(R-G)+(R-B)]}{\\sqrt{(R-G)^2+(R-B)(G-B)}}\\Big)$. Hue is undefined when $S=0$, saturation is undefined when $I=0$.",
    "hint": "If you make the night frame brighter, which of hue, saturation and intensity should not move?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$I=(R+G+B)/3$ = brightness.</strong> The plain average of the three channels, the grey level of the pixel.",
      "<strong>$S=1-3\\min(R,G,B)/(R+G+B)$ = distance from grey.</strong> Take away the grey part (the smallest channel) and see how much is left: a grey pixel has $S=0$.",
      "<strong>$H=\\theta$ or $360^\\circ-\\theta$ = the angle on the colour wheel.</strong> It names which pure colour (red, green, blue, ...) and does not change when brightness changes."
    ],
