    "highlighterClass": "highlight-amber",
    "title": "Point Operations: s = T(r)",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-3022\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"24.0\" y1=\"116.0\" x2=\"130.0\" y2=\"116.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-3022)\"/><line x1=\"24.0\" y1=\"116.0\" x2=\"24.0\" y2=\"18.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-3022)\"/><text x=\"132\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">r</text><text x=\"16\" y=\"18\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">s</text><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"116\" x2=\"114\" y2=\"26\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.6\" stroke-dasharray=\"2 3\"/><path d=\"M24.0,116.0 L26.2,98.9 L28.5,92.6 L30.8,87.9 L33.0,84.1 L35.2,80.7 L37.5,77.7 L39.8,74.9 L42.0,72.4 L44.2,70.0 L46.5,67.8 L48.8,65.7 L51.0,63.6 L53.2,61.7 L55.5,59.9 L57.8,58.1 L60.0,56.4 L62.2,54.8 L64.5,53.2 L66.8,51.6 L69.0,50.1 L71.2,48.7 L73.5,47.2 L75.8,45.8 L78.0,44.5 L80.2,43.2 L82.5,41.9 L84.8,40.6 L87.0,39.3 L89.2,38.1 L91.5,36.9 L93.8,35.8 L96.0,34.6 L98.2,33.5 L100.5,32.3 L102.8,31.2 L105.0,30.2 L107.2,29.1 L109.5,28.1 L111.8,27.0 L114.0,26.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"40\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03b3 &lt; 1 brightens</text><path d=\"M24.0,116.0 L26.2,116.0 L28.5,115.9 L30.8,115.7 L33.0,115.4 L35.2,115.1 L37.5,114.6 L39.8,114.1 L42.0,113.4 L44.2,112.6 L46.5,111.7 L48.8,110.7 L51.0,109.6 L53.2,108.4 L55.5,107.1 L57.8,105.6 L60.0,104.0 L62.2,102.3 L64.5,100.5 L66.8,98.5 L69.0,96.4 L71.2,94.2 L73.5,91.8 L75.8,89.4 L78.0,86.7 L80.2,84.0 L82.5,81.1 L84.8,78.1 L87.0,74.9 L89.2,71.6 L91.5,68.2 L93.8,64.6 L96.0,60.9 L98.2,57.1 L100.5,53.1 L102.8,48.9 L105.0,44.6 L107.2,40.2 L109.5,35.6 L111.8,30.9 L114.0,26.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 2\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"88\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03b3 > 1 darkens</text><path d=\"M24.0,116.0 L26.2,108.1 L28.5,101.5 L30.8,95.8 L33.0,90.9 L35.2,86.5 L37.5,82.6 L39.8,79.0 L42.0,75.8 L44.2,72.7 L46.5,69.9 L48.8,67.3 L51.0,64.9 L53.2,62.6 L55.5,60.4 L57.8,58.3 L60.0,56.4 L62.2,54.5 L64.5,52.7 L66.8,51.0 L69.0,49.4 L71.2,47.8 L73.5,46.3 L75.8,44.8 L78.0,43.4 L80.2,42.1 L82.5,40.8 L84.8,39.5 L87.0,38.3 L89.2,37.1 L91.5,36.0 L93.8,34.8 L96.0,33.8 L98.2,32.7 L100.5,31.7 L102.8,30.7 L105.0,29.7 L107.2,28.7 L109.5,27.8 L111.8,26.9 L114.0,26.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.8\" stroke-dasharray=\"1 2\"/><rect x=\"144\" y=\"22\" width=\"86\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"187\" y=\"34\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">s = T(r), same T</text><text x=\"187\" y=\"45\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">for every pixel</text><text x=\"187\" y=\"72\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">negative: s = L\u22121\u2212r</text><text x=\"187\" y=\"84\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">log: s = c\u00b7log(1+r)</text><text x=\"187\" y=\"96\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">gamma: s = c\u00b7r\u1d5e</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"138\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">brighten the night frame, pixel by pixel</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "Curves s = T(r) on the street frame: \u03b3 < 1 and the log lift dark pixels, \u03b3 > 1 darkens, the negative flips the scale. Every pixel uses the same curve.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "A <strong>point operation</strong> maps every pixel through the same function $s=T(r)$, ignoring its neighbors.",
      "<strong>Negative</strong> $s=L-1-r$, <strong>log</strong> $s=c\\log(1+r)$ stretches dark detail, and <strong>power-law (gamma)</strong> $s=c\\,r^{\\gamma}$ brightens ($\\gamma<1$) or darkens ($\\gamma>1$).",
      "<strong>Contrast stretching</strong> uses a piecewise-linear $T$ to spread a narrow gray range across the full scale."
    ],
    "math": "$$s=T(r),\\quad s=c\\,r^{\\gamma},\\quad s=c\\log(1+r),\\quad s=\\frac{r-r_{\\min}}{r_{\\max}-r_{\\min}}(L-1)$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Brightening the night footage.</strong> Run every pixel of the dim street frame through the same bent curve: shadows lift, the lamp stays bright. A pixel that was already black cannot be recovered, because the curve only moves values.",
    "examTrap": "Normalize r to [0, 1] before applying a gamma, or c must absorb the (L\u22121)^(1\u2212\u03b3) scale. Also a point operation can never recover detail already clipped to one level.",
    "stmtKind": "DEFINITION",
    "statement": "<b>Point (intensity) transformation.</b> A point operation replaces each pixel value $r$ by $s=T(r)$, with the same function $T$ for every pixel and independent of neighbours. Standard choices on $[0,L-1]$: negative $s=L-1-r$; log $s=c\\log(1+r)$; power law $s=c\\,r^{\\gamma}$ ($\\gamma\\lt1$ brightens, $\\gamma\\gt1$ darkens); contrast stretching $s=\\frac{r-r_{\\min}}{r_{\\max}-r_{\\min}}(L-1)$.",
    "hint": "Which curve would you bend to lift the dark street without touching the lamps?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$s=T(r)$ = one rule for every pixel.</strong> Each pixel looks only at its own value; its neighbours play no part.",
      "<strong>$c\\,r^{\\gamma}$ and $c\\log(1+r)$ = lift the dark end.</strong> For $\\gamma\\lt1$ and the log, dark values are spread out and bright ones are squeezed together.",
      "<strong>$\\frac{r-r_{\\min}}{r_{\\max}-r_{\\min}}(L-1)$ = stretch the used range.</strong> Move the darkest value in the frame to 0 and the brightest to $L-1$."
    ],
