    "highlighterClass": "highlight-purple",
    "title": "Otsu: Maximize Between-Class Variance",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-3024\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"14.0\" y1=\"84.0\" x2=\"150.0\" y2=\"84.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-3024)\"/><line x1=\"14.0\" y1=\"84.0\" x2=\"14.0\" y2=\"12.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-3024)\"/><text x=\"150\" y=\"94\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">k</text><path d=\"M18.0,83.1 L20.1,82.4 L22.3,81.2 L24.4,79.4 L26.5,76.8 L28.7,73.2 L30.8,68.6 L32.9,63.1 L35.1,56.8 L37.2,50.3 L39.3,44.1 L41.5,39.0 L43.6,35.4 L45.7,34.0 L47.9,34.9 L50.0,37.9 L52.1,42.7 L54.3,48.7 L56.4,55.2 L58.5,61.6 L60.7,67.3 L62.8,72.2 L64.9,76.0 L67.1,78.8 L69.2,80.8 L71.3,82.1 L73.5,82.8 L75.6,83.2 L77.7,83.3 L79.9,83.1 L82.0,82.6 L84.1,81.7 L86.3,80.2 L88.4,78.1 L90.5,75.1 L92.7,71.3 L94.8,66.7 L96.9,61.5 L99.1,56.0 L101.2,50.8 L103.3,46.4 L105.5,43.4 L107.6,42.0 L109.7,42.6 L111.9,45.1 L114.0,49.0 L116.1,54.0 L118.3,59.5 L120.4,64.8 L122.5,69.7 L124.7,73.8 L126.8,77.1 L128.9,79.5 L131.1,81.2 L133.2,82.4 L135.3,83.1 L137.5,83.5 L139.6,83.7 L141.7,83.9 L143.9,83.9 L146.0,84.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"78\" y1=\"84\" x2=\"78\" y2=\"20\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 2\"/><text x=\"78\" y=\"16\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">k</text><text x=\"46\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03c9\u2080</text><text x=\"108\" y=\"36\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03c9\u2081</text><circle cx=\"46.0\" cy=\"92.0\" r=\"1.6\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"108.0\" cy=\"92.0\" r=\"1.6\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"46\" y=\"102\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03bc\u2080</text><text x=\"108\" y=\"102\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03bc\u2081</text><line x1=\"46\" y1=\"116\" x2=\"108\" y2=\"116\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/><line x1=\"46\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"46\" y2=\"120\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/><line x1=\"108\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"108\" y2=\"120\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/><text x=\"77\" y=\"128\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03bc\u2080 \u2212 \u03bc\u2081</text><rect x=\"164\" y=\"20\" width=\"66\" height=\"62\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"197\" y=\"34\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03c3B\u00b2(k) =</text><text x=\"197\" y=\"46\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03c9\u2080 \u03c9\u2081</text><text x=\"197\" y=\"58\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">(\u03bc\u2080 \u2212 \u03bc\u2081)\u00b2</text><text x=\"197\" y=\"74\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">big = well split</text><text x=\"197\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">k* = argmax \u03c3B\u00b2</text><text x=\"197\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">= min within-class</text><text x=\"197\" y=\"122\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">variance</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "A cut k splits the street histogram into classes with weights \u03c9\u2080, \u03c9\u2081 and means \u03bc\u2080, \u03bc\u2081. Otsu picks the k with the largest \u03c9\u2080\u03c9\u2081(\u03bc\u2080 \u2212 \u03bc\u2081)\u00b2.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "Split the histogram at a trial level $k$ into class 0 (\u2264 k) and class 1 (> k) with probabilities $\\omega_0,\\omega_1$ and means $\\mu_0,\\mu_1$.",
      "<strong>Between-class variance</strong> $\\sigma_B^2(k)=\\omega_0\\omega_1(\\mu_0-\\mu_1)^2$ is large when the classes are well separated and balanced.",
      "Since total variance is fixed, <strong>maximizing $\\sigma_B^2$ is the same as minimizing the within-class variance</strong>. Pick $k^*$ with the largest value."
    ],
    "math": "$$k^*=\\arg\\max_k\\ \\sigma_B^2(k),\\qquad \\sigma_B^2(k)=\\omega_0(k)\\,\\omega_1(k)\\,\\big[\\mu_0(k)-\\mu_1(k)\\big]^2$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Let the frame choose its own cut.</strong> Instead of guessing a brightness, try every cut on the street histogram and keep the one that separates road from people best. It fails when one side is tiny, like a single far-away person.",
    "examTrap": "Otsu assumes roughly two classes of comparable size. With one tiny object on a big background, or a unimodal histogram, it gives a bad threshold.",
    "stmtKind": "ALGORITHM",
    "statement": "<b>Otsu's method.</b> For a normalized histogram $p_i$ and a trial threshold $k$, let $\\omega_0(k)=\\sum_{i\\le k}p_i$, $\\omega_1=1-\\omega_0$, with class means $\\mu_0(k),\\mu_1(k)$. The between-class variance is $\\sigma_B^2(k)=\\omega_0\\omega_1(\\mu_0-\\mu_1)^2$. Otsu's threshold is $k^*=\\arg\\max_k\\sigma_B^2(k)$, which also minimizes the within-class variance because the total variance is fixed.",
    "hint": "Which cut makes the two groups of pixels as far apart and as balanced as possible?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$\\omega_0,\\omega_1$ = how many pixels are on each side of the cut.</strong> The two shares of the frame, adding to 1.",
      "<strong>$(\\mu_0-\\mu_1)^2$ = how far apart the two groups are.</strong> The squared gap between their average brightnesses.",
      "<strong>$\\arg\\max_k\\,\\omega_0\\omega_1(\\mu_0-\\mu_1)^2$ = the best cut.</strong> A big gap and balanced groups give a large value; the cut with the largest value wins."
    ],
