    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-3025\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"18.0\" y1=\"100.0\" x2=\"150.0\" y2=\"100.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-3025)\"/><line x1=\"18.0\" y1=\"100.0\" x2=\"18.0\" y2=\"14.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-3025)\"/><text x=\"150\" y=\"110\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">k</text><path d=\"M22.0,99.9 L24.1,99.9 L26.1,99.8 L28.2,99.7 L30.3,99.7 L32.3,99.6 L34.4,99.5 L36.5,99.3 L38.5,99.1 L40.6,98.8 L42.7,98.5 L44.7,98.1 L46.8,97.6 L48.9,96.9 L50.9,96.0 L53.0,95.0 L55.1,93.7 L57.1,92.2 L59.2,90.4 L61.3,88.2 L63.3,85.8 L65.4,83.1 L67.5,80.2 L69.5,77.2 L71.6,74.2 L73.7,71.3 L75.7,68.5 L77.8,65.9 L79.9,63.6 L81.9,61.5 L84.0,59.7 L86.1,58.2 L88.1,56.8 L90.2,55.6 L92.3,54.4 L94.3,53.3 L96.4,52.0 L98.5,50.7 L100.5,49.1 L102.6,47.2 L104.7,45.1 L106.7,42.7 L108.8,40.1 L110.9,37.4 L112.9,34.8 L115.0,32.5 L117.1,30.4 L119.1,28.7 L121.2,27.3 L123.3,26.2 L125.3,25.4 L127.4,24.8 L129.5,24.4 L131.5,24.0 L133.6,23.8 L135.7,23.6 L137.7,23.5 L139.8,23.4 L141.9,23.4 L143.9,23.3 L146.0,23.3\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"26\" y=\"38\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03c9(k) = \u03a3 p\u1d62</text><line x1=\"84\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"84\" y2=\"30\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 2\"/><text x=\"84\" y=\"110\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">k</text><circle cx=\"84.0\" cy=\"54.0\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"88\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03bc(k)</text><line x1=\"18\" y1=\"24\" x2=\"146\" y2=\"24\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.6\" stroke-dasharray=\"1 3\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"20\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03bcT</text><rect x=\"162\" y=\"20\" width=\"68\" height=\"70\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"196\" y=\"34\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03c3B\u00b2(k) =</text><text x=\"196\" y=\"46\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">[\u03bcT\u00b7\u03c9 \u2212 \u03bc]\u00b2</text><line x1=\"170\" y1=\"51\" x2=\"222\" y2=\"51\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/><text x=\"196\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03c9 (1 \u2212 \u03c9)</text><text x=\"196\" y=\"80\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">one pass: O(L)</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"128\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">running totals along the histogram of the frame</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "Walking along the street histogram we keep \u03c9(k) (running share) and \u03bc(k) (running mean); with the total mean \u03bcT they give \u03c3B\u00b2(k) in one pass.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "Precompute cumulative <strong>$\\omega(k)=\\sum_{i\\le k}p_i$</strong> and <strong>$\\mu(k)=\\sum_{i\\le k}i\\,p_i$</strong>, with total mean $\\mu_T=\\mu(L-1)$.",
      "Then $\\sigma_B^2(k)=\\dfrac{[\\mu_T\\omega(k)-\\mu(k)]^2}{\\omega(k)[1-\\omega(k)]}$ costs only <strong>O(L)</strong>: one pass over the histogram.",
      "If several $k$ tie (empty histogram bins between modes), <strong>average the tied $k$ values</strong> to get the threshold."
    ],
    "math": "$$\\sigma_B^2(k)=\\frac{\\big[\\mu_T\\,\\omega(k)-\\mu(k)\\big]^2}{\\omega(k)\\,[1-\\omega(k)]},\\quad k^*=\\arg\\max_k\\sigma_B^2(k)$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>One sweep along the night histogram.</strong> Keep two running totals as you walk from black to white and read the score of every cut off them, instead of recomputing the two groups each time.",
    "examTrap": "Divide-by-zero at \u03c9(k) = 0 or 1: skip those k. And report the middle of a plateau, not just the first maximum.",
    "stmtKind": "PROPOSITION",
    "statement": "<b>Otsu with cumulative sums.</b> Let $\\omega(k)=\\sum_{i\\le k}p_i$, $\\mu(k)=\\sum_{i\\le k}i\\,p_i$ and $\\mu_T=\\mu(L-1)$. Then $\\sigma_B^2(k)=\\dfrac{[\\mu_T\\,\\omega(k)-\\mu(k)]^2}{\\omega(k)\\,[1-\\omega(k)]}$ for $0\\lt\\omega(k)\\lt1$, so all $L$ values are computed in one pass, and $k^*=\\arg\\max_k\\sigma_B^2(k)$; if several $k$ tie, their average is taken.",
    "hint": "How can you score every possible cut by sweeping once along the histogram?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$\\omega(k)$ = running share of pixels up to $k$.</strong> The fraction of the frame at or below the cut.",
      "<strong>$\\mu(k)$ = running sum of level \u00d7 share.</strong> With $\\mu_T$ (the whole frame's mean) it gives both class means without a second pass.",
      "<strong>$\\omega(1-\\omega)$ in the denominator = the balance term.</strong> It is zero when one class is empty, so those $k$ are skipped."
    ],
