    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-3042\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"18.0\" y1=\"112.0\" x2=\"130.0\" y2=\"112.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-3042)\"/><line x1=\"18.0\" y1=\"112.0\" x2=\"18.0\" y2=\"14.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-3042)\"/><text x=\"130\" y=\"122\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">r</text><text x=\"14\" y=\"18\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">s</text><path d=\"M22.0,110.3 L24.1,110.0 L26.2,109.7 L28.2,109.3 L30.3,108.7 L32.4,108.2 L34.5,107.5 L36.6,106.7 L38.6,105.7 L40.7,104.6 L42.8,103.4 L44.9,101.9 L47.0,100.2 L49.0,98.3 L51.1,96.2 L53.2,93.8 L55.3,91.1 L57.4,88.2 L59.4,85.0 L61.5,81.6 L63.6,78.0 L65.7,74.2 L67.8,70.3 L69.8,66.3 L71.9,62.3 L74.0,58.4 L76.1,54.6 L78.2,50.9 L80.2,47.5 L82.3,44.3 L84.4,41.3 L86.5,38.6 L88.6,36.2 L90.6,34.0 L92.7,32.0 L94.8,30.3 L96.9,28.9 L99.0,27.6 L101.0,26.4 L103.1,25.5 L105.2,24.6 L107.3,23.9 L109.4,23.3 L111.4,22.8 L113.5,22.4 L115.6,22.0 L117.7,21.7 L119.8,21.4 L121.8,21.2 L123.9,21.0 L126.0,20.9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"70\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"70\" y2=\"66\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.6\" stroke-dasharray=\"2 3\"/><line x1=\"18\" y1=\"66\" x2=\"70\" y2=\"66\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.6\" stroke-dasharray=\"2 3\"/><text x=\"78\" y=\"56\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">slope = (L\u22121)\u00b7p(r)</text><text x=\"70\" y=\"122\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">r</text><path d=\"M22.0,112.0 L24.6,112.0 L27.2,111.9 L29.8,111.9 L32.4,111.7 L35.0,111.5 L37.6,111.2 L40.2,110.7 L42.8,110.0 L45.4,108.9 L48.0,107.5 L50.6,105.7 L53.2,103.6 L55.8,101.3 L58.4,98.8 L61.0,96.4 L63.6,94.4 L66.2,92.9 L68.8,92.1 L71.4,92.1 L74.0,93.0 L76.6,94.5 L79.2,96.6 L81.8,99.0 L84.4,101.5 L87.0,103.8 L89.6,105.9 L92.2,107.6 L94.8,109.0 L97.4,110.0 L100.0,110.8 L102.6,111.2 L105.2,111.6 L107.8,111.8 L110.4,111.9 L113.0,111.9 L115.6,112.0 L118.2,112.0 L120.8,112.0 L123.4,112.0 L126.0,112.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.8\" stroke-dasharray=\"2 2\"/><text x=\"44\" y=\"98\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">p(r)</text><rect x=\"148\" y=\"20\" width=\"82\" height=\"74\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"189\" y=\"34\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">ds/dr = (L\u22121)\u00b7p(r)</text><text x=\"189\" y=\"50\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">p(s) = p(r)\u00b7|dr/ds|</text><text x=\"189\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">= 1/(L\u22121)</text><text x=\"189\" y=\"84\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">flat \u2713</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"138\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">busy grey levels get a steep slope: they spread out</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "The S-curve s = T(r) is the running total of p(r). Its slope (L\u22121)\u00b7p(r) is steep where the histogram is tall, which cancels the crowding and makes p(s) = 1/(L\u22121).",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "Let $s=T(r)=(L-1)\\int_0^r p_r(w)\\,dw$. This $T$ is <strong>monotonically increasing</strong> and maps $[0,L-1]$ onto itself.",
      "By the change-of-variables rule, $p_s(s)=p_r(r)\\left|\\dfrac{dr}{ds}\\right|$ and $\\dfrac{ds}{dr}=(L-1)p_r(r)$, so <strong>$p_s(s)=\\dfrac{1}{L-1}$</strong>: uniform.",
      "In words: the transform is the 'probability integral transform'; pushing a random variable through its own CDF yields a uniform one."
    ],
    "math": "$$\\frac{ds}{dr}=(L-1)\\,p_r(r)\\ \\Rightarrow\\ p_s(s)=p_r(r)\\Big|\\frac{dr}{ds}\\Big|=\\frac{1}{L-1}$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Why the lamp area is not overstretched.</strong> The curve is steepest where the night frame has most pixels and gentle where it has few, so crowded dark levels get as much room as the sparse bright ones.",
    "examTrap": "The proof needs a continuous, strictly increasing CDF. The discrete version is only an approximation and never gives a perfectly flat histogram.",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>Equalization gives a uniform density (probability integral transform).</b> Let $r\\in[0,L-1]$ have a continuous density $p_r$ with strictly increasing CDF, and let $s=T(r)=(L-1)\\int_0^r p_r(w)\\,dw$. Then $s$ is uniformly distributed on $[0,L-1]$: $p_s(s)=\\frac1{L-1}$.",
    "hint": "Why does pushing the grey levels through their own running total flatten the histogram?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$ds/dr=(L-1)\\,p_r(r)$ = the slope of the curve is the crowding.</strong> Where many pixels sit, the curve is steep and pulls those levels apart.",
      "<strong>$p_s(s)=p_r(r)\\,|dr/ds|$ = the change-of-variables rule.</strong> Density in the new variable is the old density divided by the stretch.",
      "<strong>$p_r\\cdot\\dfrac1{(L-1)p_r}=\\dfrac1{L-1}$ = the crowding cancels.</strong> Crowded parts are stretched exactly as much as they were crowded, so the output has equal density everywhere."
    ],
