    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-3044\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"16.0\" y1=\"112.0\" x2=\"112.0\" y2=\"112.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-3044)\"/><line x1=\"16.0\" y1=\"112.0\" x2=\"16.0\" y2=\"16.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-3044)\"/><text x=\"114\" y=\"122\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">r , z</text><text x=\"10\" y=\"18\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">level</text><path d=\"M16.0,112.0 L18.4,100.4 L20.8,95.1 L23.2,90.8 L25.6,87.2 L28.0,84.0 L30.4,81.0 L32.8,78.3 L35.2,75.7 L37.6,73.3 L40.0,70.9 L42.4,68.7 L44.8,66.6 L47.2,64.6 L49.6,62.6 L52.0,60.7 L54.4,58.8 L56.8,57.0 L59.2,55.3 L61.6,53.6 L64.0,51.9 L66.4,50.3 L68.8,48.7 L71.2,47.1 L73.6,45.6 L76.0,44.0 L78.4,42.6 L80.8,41.1 L83.2,39.7 L85.6,38.3 L88.0,36.9 L90.4,35.5 L92.8,34.2 L95.2,32.8 L97.6,31.5 L100.0,30.2 L102.4,29.0 L104.8,27.7 L107.2,26.4 L109.6,25.2 L112.0,24.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"40\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">T(r) (input CDF)</text><path d=\"M16.0,112.0 L18.4,111.9 L20.8,111.8 L23.2,111.5 L25.6,111.1 L28.0,110.6 L30.4,110.0 L32.8,109.3 L35.2,108.5 L37.6,107.5 L40.0,106.5 L42.4,105.3 L44.8,104.1 L47.2,102.7 L49.6,101.2 L52.0,99.6 L54.4,97.9 L56.8,96.1 L59.2,94.2 L61.6,92.1 L64.0,90.0 L66.4,87.7 L68.8,85.4 L71.2,82.9 L73.6,80.3 L76.0,77.6 L78.4,74.8 L80.8,71.9 L83.2,68.9 L85.6,65.7 L88.0,62.5 L90.4,59.1 L92.8,55.7 L95.2,52.1 L97.6,48.4 L100.0,44.6 L102.4,40.7 L104.8,36.7 L107.2,32.6 L109.6,28.3 L112.0,24.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 2\"/><text x=\"76\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">G(z) (target CDF)</text><circle cx=\"60.0\" cy=\"64.0\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><line x1=\"60.0\" y1=\"112.0\" x2=\"60.0\" y2=\"68.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.8\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-3044)\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"122\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">r</text><line x1=\"60.0\" y1=\"64.0\" x2=\"98.0\" y2=\"64.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.8\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-3044)\"/><line x1=\"98.0\" y1=\"64.0\" x2=\"98.0\" y2=\"112.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.8\" stroke-dasharray=\"1 2\"/><circle cx=\"98.0\" cy=\"64.0\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"98\" y=\"122\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">z</text><rect x=\"130\" y=\"20\" width=\"100\" height=\"70\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"180\" y=\"34\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">s = T(r)</text><text x=\"180\" y=\"48\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">v = G(z)</text><text x=\"180\" y=\"64\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">set s = v \u21d2</text><text x=\"180\" y=\"80\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">z = G\u207b\u00b9[T(r)]</text><text x=\"180\" y=\"108\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">match one frame's look</text><text x=\"180\" y=\"119\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">to another's</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"138\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">G is a staircase: take the z with G(z) closest to s</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "A pixel r goes up through the input CDF T to a level s, then across and down through the target CDF G (inverted) to z. The result z = G\u207b\u00b9[T(r)] has the target's histogram.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>What:</strong> Instead of a flat output, you force the histogram to match a <strong>chosen target shape</strong> $p_z(z)$.",
      "<strong>How:</strong> Equalize the input ($s=T(r)$) and equalize the target ($v=G(z)$); since both give uniform histograms, set $s=v$ and invert: <strong>$z=G^{-1}[T(r)]$</strong>.",
      "<strong>Why:</strong> It lets you match one image's look to another or shape contrast for a specific display."
    ],
    "math": "$$s=T(r)=(L-1)\\sum p_r,\\qquad G(z)=(L-1)\\sum p_z,\\qquad z=G^{-1}\\big(T(r)\\big)$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Making night footage look like a good daytime frame.</strong> Take the daytime frame's histogram as the target and push each night pixel through $T$ and then back out through $G^{-1}$.",
    "examTrap": "G is a staircase, so G\u207b\u00b9 is not exact: pick the z whose G(z) is closest to s (and handle ties consistently).",
    "stmtKind": "ALGORITHM",
    "statement": "<b>Histogram specification (matching).</b> Given an input with equalizing map $s=T(r)=(L-1)\\sum p_r$ and a desired density $p_z$ with $G(z)=(L-1)\\sum p_z$: compute $T$; compute $G$; for each $r$ output $z=G^{-1}\\big(T(r)\\big)$ (for a staircase $G$, the $z$ whose $G(z)$ is closest to $s$). The result has a histogram close to $p_z$.",
    "hint": "If flat is not what you want, how do you aim the output at the look of a different frame?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$s=T(r)$ = equalize the input.</strong> Send the frame to the flat middle ground first.",
      "<strong>$G(z)$ = equalize the target.</strong> The same trip for the histogram shape you want.",
      "<strong>$z=G^{-1}(T(r))$ = go in with $T$, come out with $G^{-1}$.</strong> Both sides pass through the same flat middle ground, so joining them matches the shapes."
    ],
