    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-3045\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><rect x=\"10\" y=\"20\" width=\"22\" height=\"22\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"42\" width=\"22\" height=\"22\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"64\" width=\"22\" height=\"22\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/><rect x=\"32\" y=\"20\" width=\"22\" height=\"22\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/><rect x=\"32\" y=\"42\" width=\"22\" height=\"22\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/><rect x=\"32\" y=\"64\" width=\"22\" height=\"22\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/><rect x=\"54\" y=\"20\" width=\"22\" height=\"22\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/><rect x=\"54\" y=\"42\" width=\"22\" height=\"22\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/><rect x=\"54\" y=\"64\" width=\"22\" height=\"22\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/><text x=\"43\" y=\"14\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">equalise each tile</text><text x=\"43\" y=\"96\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">blend neighbours</text><line x1=\"104.0\" y1=\"80.0\" x2=\"232.0\" y2=\"80.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-3045)\"/><line x1=\"104.0\" y1=\"80.0\" x2=\"104.0\" y2=\"14.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-3045)\"/><text x=\"232\" y=\"90\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">k</text><text x=\"100\" y=\"18\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">h(k)</text><path d=\"M110.0,80.0 L113.0,80.0 L115.9,79.8 L118.8,79.3 L121.8,77.7 L124.8,73.9 L127.7,66.3 L130.7,54.1 L133.6,38.8 L136.6,25.0 L139.5,18.2 L142.4,21.6 L145.4,33.7 L148.3,49.1 L151.3,62.7 L154.2,71.9 L157.2,76.8 L160.2,78.9 L163.1,79.7 L166.1,79.9 L169.0,80.0 L171.9,80.0 L174.9,80.0 L177.8,80.0 L180.8,80.0 L183.8,80.0 L186.7,80.0 L189.7,80.0 L192.6,80.0 L195.6,80.0 L198.5,80.0 L201.4,80.0 L204.4,80.0 L207.3,80.0 L210.3,80.0 L213.2,80.0 L216.2,80.0 L219.2,80.0 L222.1,80.0 L225.1,80.0 L228.0,80.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"110\" y1=\"36\" x2=\"228\" y2=\"36\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.8\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 2\"/><text x=\"228\" y=\"46\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03b2 (clip)</text><rect x=\"131\" y=\"24\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#d9dee7\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.6\"/><text x=\"158\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">excess \u21d2 spread</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">hclip(k) = min(h(k), \u03b2)</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"126\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">excess = \u03a3 (h(k) \u2212 \u03b2)\u207a , redistributed evenly</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">without the clip, flat tiles turn into noise</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "Each tile of the frame has its own histogram h(k). Bars above the clip limit \u03b2 are cut and the excess is spread over all bins; neighbouring tiles are then blended.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Local (adaptive) HE</strong> equalizes each small tile separately, boosting <strong>local contrast</strong> that global HE misses.",
      "Plain local HE <strong>amplifies noise</strong> in flat tiles because a tall narrow peak maps to a steep slope.",
      "<strong>CLAHE</strong> clips the histogram at a limit, spreads the clipped excess across all bins, and <strong>bilinearly blends neighboring tiles</strong> to hide seams."
    ],
    "math": "$$h_{\\text{clip}}(k)=\\min\\big(h(k),\\,\\beta\\big),\\qquad \\text{excess}=\\sum_k\\big(h(k)-\\beta\\big)^+\\ \\text{redistributed uniformly}$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Dark alley, bright shopfront.</strong> One curve for the whole frame cannot serve both. Tiles fix that; the clip stops the blank wall of the building from turning into grain.",
    "examTrap": "Without the clip limit, local equalization turns uniform regions into noise. The clip limit is what makes CLAHE usable.",
    "stmtKind": "ALGORITHM",
    "statement": "<b>Local equalization and CLAHE.</b> Local histogram equalization divides the image into tiles and equalizes each tile separately. Contrast-limited adaptive HE (CLAHE) clips each tile's histogram at a limit $\\beta$: $h_{\\rm clip}(k)=\\min(h(k),\\beta)$, redistributes the total excess $\\sum_k(h(k)-\\beta)^+$ uniformly over all bins, equalizes with the clipped histogram, and bilinearly interpolates between neighbouring tiles' mappings to remove tile seams.",
    "hint": "Why does equalizing each little tile of the frame turn flat sky into noise unless you cap the histogram?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>Tiles = equalize locally.</strong> Each patch of the frame gets its own curve, so local contrast, such as a dark alley, is boosted.",
      "<strong>$h_{\\rm clip}=\\min(h,\\beta)$ = cap the tall bars.</strong> A tall narrow bar (a flat wall) would give a very steep curve that magnifies noise; clipping limits the slope.",
      "<strong>Redistribute the excess, blend the tiles.</strong> The clipped mass is spread over all bins so no pixels are lost, and blending neighbours hides the tile edges."
    ],
