    "title": "2D DFT Definition & Separability",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-3061\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><text x=\"40.4\" y=\"12\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">fence in the frame f</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"18\" width=\"60\" height=\"44\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><rect x=\"14.6\" y=\"18\" width=\"4.6\" height=\"44\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#b8c0cc\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.5\"/><rect x=\"23.8\" y=\"18\" width=\"4.6\" height=\"44\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#b8c0cc\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.5\"/><rect x=\"33.1\" y=\"18\" width=\"4.6\" height=\"44\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#b8c0cc\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.5\"/><rect x=\"42.3\" y=\"18\" width=\"4.6\" height=\"44\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#b8c0cc\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.5\"/><rect x=\"51.5\" y=\"18\" width=\"4.6\" height=\"44\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#b8c0cc\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.5\"/><rect x=\"60.8\" y=\"18\" width=\"4.6\" height=\"44\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#b8c0cc\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.5\"/><text x=\"40\" y=\"74\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">6 stripes across</text><line x1=\"74.0\" y1=\"40.0\" x2=\"98.0\" y2=\"40.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-3061)\"/><text x=\"86\" y=\"34\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">DFT</text><text x=\"160\" y=\"12\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">F(u, v)</text><rect x=\"104\" y=\"18\" width=\"112\" height=\"44\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><circle cx=\"160\" cy=\"40\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"184\" cy=\"40\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><circle cx=\"136\" cy=\"40\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"160\" y=\"54\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">DC</text><text x=\"184\" y=\"34\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">u = 6</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"92\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">F(u,v) = \u03a3\u03a3 f(x,y) e^(\u2212j2\u03c0(ux/M + vy/N))</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"106\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">kernel = row wave \u00d7 column wave \u21d2 rows, then columns</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"120\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">FFT: O(MN log MN)</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"134\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">the fence = one pair of bright dots</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "A fence of 6 stripes across the street frame f gives F(u, v) with a bright dot at the origin (DC) and a pair at u = \u00b16. F(u,v) = \u03a3\u03a3 f(x,y)\u00b7e^(\u2212j2\u03c0(ux/M + vy/N)).",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "The 2D DFT of an $M\\times N$ image decomposes the image into <strong>2D complex sinusoids</strong> of frequency $(u/M,\\,v/N)$.",
      "The kernel <strong>factors</strong>: $e^{-j2\\pi(ux/M+vy/N)}=e^{-j2\\pi ux/M}\\,e^{-j2\\pi vy/N}$, so compute 1D DFTs along rows, then along columns (in either order).",
      "With the FFT, this costs <strong>O(MN log MN)</strong>, so frequency-domain filtering is practical on large images."
    ],
    "math": "$$F(u,v)=\\sum_{x=0}^{M-1}\\sum_{y=0}^{N-1}f(x,y)\\,e^{-j2\\pi\\left(\\frac{ux}{M}+\\frac{vy}{N}\\right)},\\quad f(x,y)=\\frac{1}{MN}\\sum_{u,v}F(u,v)e^{j2\\pi\\left(\\frac{ux}{M}+\\frac{vy}{N}\\right)}$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>The fence in the street.</strong> A fence with six stripes across the frame shows up as one pair of bright dots at $u=\\pm6$: the DFT says how much of each stripe pattern the frame holds, and nothing about where the fence is.",
    "examTrap": "The inverse carries the 1/(MN) factor, but some textbooks put 1/\u221a(MN) on both transforms. State your normalization when comparing numbers.",
    "stmtKind": "DEFINITION",
    "statement": "<b>2D discrete Fourier transform.</b> For an $M\\times N$ image $f(x,y)$, $F(u,v)=\\sum_{x=0}^{M-1}\\sum_{y=0}^{N-1}f(x,y)\\,e^{-j2\\pi(ux/M+vy/N)}$, with inverse $f(x,y)=\\frac1{MN}\\sum_{u,v}F(u,v)\\,e^{j2\\pi(ux/M+vy/N)}$. The kernel is separable, so $F$ is computed by 1D DFTs along the rows and then along the columns, and with the FFT in $O(MN\\log MN)$ operations.",
    "hint": "Which two bright dots would the fence's stripes put in the frequency picture?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$e^{-j2\\pi(ux/M+vy/N)}$ = a wave of frequency $(u,v)$.</strong> A stripe pattern across the frame; $u$ counts stripes along $x$, $v$ along $y$.",
      "<strong>$\\sum\\sum f(x,y)\\,e^{-j2\\pi(\\cdot)}$ = how much of that wave the frame contains.</strong> Multiply the frame by the wave and add up: a big total means the frame has that stripe pattern.",
      "<strong>Separable kernel = rows, then columns.</strong> The 2D wave is a product of a row wave and a column wave, so two sweeps of the 1D FFT give $F$ cheaply."
    ],
