    "examTrap": "Do not conclude magnitude is useless: it still sets contrast and texture energy. Only that structure, position and edges are carried by phase.",
    "stmtKind": "PROPOSITION",
    "statement": "<b>Magnitude and phase.</b> Writing $F(u,v)=|F(u,v)|\\,e^{j\\angle F(u,v)}$, the magnitude gives the amplitude of each frequency component and the phase gives its alignment. Reconstruction from the phase alone, $\\mathcal F^{-1}\\{e^{j\\angle F}\\}$, retains the edges and structure of $f$, while reconstruction from the magnitude alone, $\\mathcal F^{-1}\\{|F|\\}$, does not; exchanging the phases of two images makes each result resemble the image that supplied the phase.",
