    "statement": "<b>Convolution theorem.</b> For the DFT, $\\mathcal F\\{f\\circledast h\\}=F(u,v)\\,H(u,v)$, where $\\circledast$ is circular convolution of period $(P,Q)$. If $f$ has size $M$ and $h$ size $K$ (in each dimension) and both are zero-padded to $P\\ge M+K-1$, then the circular convolution equals the linear convolution $f\\ast h$.",
