    "title": "Nyquist: f_s \u2265 2 f_max",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-3072\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><text x=\"12\" y=\"12\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">f\u209b \u2265 2 f\u2098\u2090\u2093</text><line x1=\"10.0\" y1=\"44.0\" x2=\"232.0\" y2=\"44.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-3072)\"/><line x1=\"10.0\" y1=\"44.0\" x2=\"10.0\" y2=\"12.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-3072)\"/><path d=\"M26.0,44.0 L40.0,18.0 L54.0,44.0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><path d=\"M106.0,44.0 L120.0,18.0 L134.0,44.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 2\"/><path d=\"M186.0,44.0 L200.0,18.0 L214.0,44.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 2\"/><text x=\"40\" y=\"54\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">f\u2098\u2090\u2093</text><line x1=\"40\" y1=\"14\" x2=\"40\" y2=\"14\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.5\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"54\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">gap \u21d2 cut out the middle copy</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">f\u209b &lt; 2 f\u2098\u2090\u2093</text><line x1=\"10.0\" y1=\"108.0\" x2=\"232.0\" y2=\"108.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-3072)\"/><line x1=\"10.0\" y1=\"108.0\" x2=\"10.0\" y2=\"74.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-3072)\"/><path d=\"M16.0,108.0 L40.0,82.0 L64.0,108.0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><path d=\"M66.0,108.0 L90.0,82.0 L114.0,108.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 2\"/><path d=\"M116.0,108.0 L140.0,82.0 L164.0,108.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 2\"/><text x=\"65\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">overlap</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"118\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">copies overlap \u21d2 aliasing</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"134\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">enough frames per second \u21d2 exact recovery</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "Top: the copies of the spectrum stay apart when f\u209b \u2265 2 f\u2098\u2090\u2093 and the middle copy can be cut out. Bottom: for smaller f\u209b the copies overlap and cause aliasing.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Condition:</strong> an image bandlimited to $|u|\\le u_{\\max}$ must be sampled at <strong>$f_s\\ge 2u_{\\max}$</strong> (Nyquist rate) in each direction: $\\Delta x\\le\\frac1{2u_{\\max}}$.",
      "<strong>If it holds</strong> the replicas don't touch and an ideal LPF (sinc interpolation) <strong>reconstructs the original exactly</strong>.",
      "<strong>If it fails</strong> the replicas overlap and high frequencies masquerade as low ones: <strong>aliasing</strong>, an irreversible loss."
    ],
    "math": "$$f_s\\ge 2f_{\\max},\\qquad f(x)=\\sum_n f(n\\Delta)\\,\\operatorname{sinc}\\!\\left(\\frac{x-n\\Delta}{\\Delta}\\right)$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>How many pixels the fence needs.</strong> The finest stripes of the fence need at least two pixels per stripe pair. Fewer, and the camera cannot tell them from something coarser.",
    "examTrap": "Nyquist rate is 2\u00b7f_max, while the Nyquist FREQUENCY is f_s/2. And the condition is for bandlimited signals; real images are not exactly bandlimited, hence prefiltering.",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>Sampling theorem (Shannon\u2013Nyquist).</b> If $f$ is bandlimited, $F(u)=0$ for $|u|\\gt u_{\\max}$, and it is sampled with spacing $\\Delta$ such that $f_s=1/\\Delta\\ge 2u_{\\max}$, then $f$ is recovered exactly from its samples: $f(x)=\\sum_n f(n\\Delta)\\,\\operatorname{sinc}\\!\\big(\\frac{x-n\\Delta}{\\Delta}\\big)$. If $f_s\\lt2u_{\\max}$ the replicas overlap and aliasing occurs.",
    "hint": "How many samples per cycle of the fence's finest stripes are the least you can get away with?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$f_s\\ge2u_{\\max}$ = at least two samples per cycle.</strong> The spacing between spectrum copies must be at least twice the highest frequency, so the copies do not overlap.",
      "<strong>$\\operatorname{sinc}\\!\\big(\\frac{x-n\\Delta}{\\Delta}\\big)$ = the ideal rebuilding bump.</strong> Putting one at each sample, scaled by the sample value, and adding gives the original exactly.",
      "<strong>$f_s\\lt2u_{\\max}$ = overlap.</strong> The copies of the spectrum touch, high frequencies pretend to be low ones and the loss cannot be undone."
    ],
