    "highlighterClass": "highlight-purple",
    "title": "Downsampling by M (Decimation)",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-3074\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><text x=\"14\" y=\"10\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">before</text><line x1=\"10.0\" y1=\"62.0\" x2=\"112.0\" y2=\"62.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-3074)\"/><line x1=\"10.0\" y1=\"62.0\" x2=\"10.0\" y2=\"14.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-3074)\"/><path d=\"M33.0,62.0 L61.0,28.0 L89.0,62.0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"61\" y=\"71\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">band up to \u03c0</text><line x1=\"116.0\" y1=\"40.0\" x2=\"130.0\" y2=\"40.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-3074)\"/><text x=\"122\" y=\"32\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\u2193M</text><text x=\"136\" y=\"10\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">after (M = 2)</text><line x1=\"132.0\" y1=\"62.0\" x2=\"232.0\" y2=\"62.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-3074)\"/><line x1=\"132.0\" y1=\"62.0\" x2=\"132.0\" y2=\"14.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-3074)\"/><path d=\"M138.0,62.0 L160.0,32.0 L182.0,62.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 2\"/><path d=\"M184.0,62.0 L206.0,32.0 L228.0,62.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 2\"/><path d=\"M161.0,62.0 L183.0,32.0 L205.0,62.0\" fill=\"#d9dee7\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"183\" y=\"71\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">copies add \u21d2 alias</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"92\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">y[n] = x[Mn]</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"105\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">Y(\u03c9) = (1/M) \u03a3 X((\u03c9 \u2212 2\u03c0k)/M)</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"120\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">filter first: low-pass with cutoff \u03c0/M</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"133\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">then drop frames: every M-th frame kept</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "A spectrum before and after dropping every other sample (M = 2): the stretched copies overlap and add, so the content beyond \u03c0/M aliases; filter first.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>What:</strong> Downsampling keeps every $M$-th sample, shrinking the image (or signal) by $M$.",
      "<strong>Spectral effect:</strong> the spectrum is <strong>stretched by M</strong> and $M$ shifted copies add together, so any content above $\\pi/M$ aliases into the baseband.",
      "<strong>Recipe:</strong> always apply an LPF with cutoff $\\pi/M$ first. This pair is called <strong>decimation</strong>."
    ],
    "math": "$$y[n]=x[Mn],\\qquad Y(\\omega)=\\frac1M\\sum_{k=0}^{M-1}X\\!\\left(\\frac{\\omega-2\\pi k}{M}\\right)$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Making a thumbnail of the street frame.</strong> Blur first, then keep every second pixel. Keeping every second pixel of the sharp frame turns the fine brick pattern into false coarse stripes.",
    "examTrap": "Dropping samples without the LPF is the textbook aliasing mistake. Also downsampling is NOT shift-invariant (time-varying).",
    "stmtKind": "DEFINITION",
    "statement": "<b>Downsampling (decimation) by $M$.</b> $y[n]=x[Mn]$. Its spectrum is $Y(\\omega)=\\frac1M\\sum_{k=0}^{M-1}X\\!\\big(\\frac{\\omega-2\\pi k}{M}\\big)$: the spectrum is stretched by $M$ and $M$ shifted copies are added, so content above $\\pi/M$ aliases. Decimation therefore applies a low-pass filter with cutoff $\\pi/M$ before discarding samples.",
    "hint": "Why must the frame be blurred a little before you throw away every other frame or pixel?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$y[n]=x[Mn]$ = keep one sample in $M$.</strong> The signal or frame shrinks by $M$, which is the same as sampling again at a lower rate.",
      "<strong>$X((\\omega-2\\pi k)/M)$ = $M$ stretched copies.</strong> Each copy is spread out by $M$ and moved by a multiple of $2\\pi$; the $M$ copies add together.",
      "<strong>Cutoff $\\pi/M$ = keep only what survives.</strong> After the stretch only the band up to $\\pi/M$ fits without overlapping; the low-pass removes the rest first."
    ],
    "textbookImg": null,
    "textbookRef": null
