    "title": "Worked Benchmark: 90 Hz Sampled at 100 Hz",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-3076\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"14\" y1=\"60\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"60\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"14\" y1=\"56\" x2=\"14\" y2=\"64\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"226\" y1=\"56\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"64\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"14\" y=\"74\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">0</text><text x=\"226\" y=\"74\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">100 Hz = f\u209b</text><line x1=\"120\" y1=\"52\" x2=\"120\" y2=\"68\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 2\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"82\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">50 = f\u209b/2</text><circle cx=\"196\" cy=\"60\" r=\"2.4\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"196\" y=\"50\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">90</text><circle cx=\"44\" cy=\"60\" r=\"2.4\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"44\" y=\"74\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">10</text><path d=\"M196,52 Q120,12 46,52\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-3076)\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">fold about f\u209b/2</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"102\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">cos(2\u03c0\u00b790\u00b7n/100) = cos(2\u03c0\u00b710\u00b7n/100)</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">k = round(90/100) = 1 \u21d2 |90 \u2212 100| = 10 Hz</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"129\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">wheel at 0.8 cycles/pixel \u21d2 |0.8 \u2212 1| = 0.2 (moir\u00e9)</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "The frequency axis from 0 to f\u209b = 100 Hz folds about f\u209b/2 = 50 Hz: 90 Hz lands on 10 Hz, and 0.8 cycles/pixel lands on 0.2.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "A <strong>90 Hz</strong> cosine sampled at $f_s=100$ Hz has $f>f_s/2=50$ Hz, so it violates Nyquist.",
      "<strong>Fold it:</strong> $k=\\operatorname{round}(90/100)=1$, so $f_{\\text{alias}}=|90-100|=\\mathbf{10\\ Hz}$. The sampled sequence is <strong>identical</strong> to that of a 10 Hz cosine.",
      "<strong>Image version:</strong> a sinusoidal grating at 0.8 cycles/pixel (above 0.5) aliases to $|0.8-1|=0.2$ cycles/pixel, visible as a coarse moir\u00e9 band."
    ],
    "math": "$$\\cos(2\\pi\\cdot90\\,\\tfrac{n}{100})=\\cos(2\\pi\\cdot(-10)\\,\\tfrac{n}{100})=\\cos(2\\pi\\cdot10\\,\\tfrac{n}{100})$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>A wheel spinning at 90 turns a second.</strong> Filmed at 100 frames a second it looks like it turns at 10, the same as a slow wheel. The 0.8 cycles/pixel brick pattern looks like a coarse band.",
    "examTrap": "The alias frequency uses the NEAREST multiple of f_s, not always k = 1. For f = 160 at f_s = 100: |160 \u2212 200| = 40 Hz, not 60.",
    "stmtKind": "WORKED EXAMPLE",
    "statement": "<b>Example.</b> A $90$ Hz cosine sampled at $f_s=100$ Hz exceeds the Nyquist frequency $f_s/2=50$ Hz. With $k=\\operatorname{round}(90/100)=1$, $f_{\\rm alias}=|90-100|=10$ Hz, and $\\cos(2\\pi\\cdot90\\,\\tfrac n{100})=\\cos(2\\pi\\cdot10\\,\\tfrac n{100})$ for every integer $n$. Likewise a grating of $0.8$ cycles/pixel aliases to $|0.8-1|=0.2$ cycles/pixel.",
    "hint": "Where does 90 Hz land when the camera only takes 100 frames a second?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$f=90\\gt f_s/2=50$ = past the fold.</strong> Above half the frame rate, so Nyquist is violated.",
      "<strong>$f_{\\rm alias}=|90-100|=10$ Hz = the nearest multiple of $f_s$.</strong> The sampled sequence is identical to that of a 10 Hz cosine.",
      "<strong>Use the nearest multiple, not always $k=1$.</strong> For $f=160$ at $f_s=100$ the fold gives $|160-200|=40$ Hz, not 60."
    ],
