    "title": "Two-Channel Filter Bank & Haar",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-3093\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><text x=\"14\" y=\"54\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">x</text><line x1=\"22.0\" y1=\"50.0\" x2=\"40.0\" y2=\"30.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-3093)\"/><line x1=\"22.0\" y1=\"50.0\" x2=\"40.0\" y2=\"70.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-3093)\"/><rect x=\"40\" y=\"22\" width=\"28\" height=\"16\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"54\" y=\"33\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">h\u2080</text><line x1=\"68.0\" y1=\"30.0\" x2=\"82.0\" y2=\"30.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-3093)\"/><rect x=\"82\" y=\"22\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"92\" y=\"33\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\u21932</text><line x1=\"102.0\" y1=\"30.0\" x2=\"116.0\" y2=\"30.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-3093)\"/><text x=\"122\" y=\"34\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">a</text><rect x=\"40\" y=\"62\" width=\"28\" height=\"16\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"54\" y=\"73\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">h\u2081</text><line x1=\"68.0\" y1=\"70.0\" x2=\"82.0\" y2=\"70.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-3093)\"/><rect x=\"82\" y=\"62\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"92\" y=\"73\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\u21932</text><line x1=\"102.0\" y1=\"70.0\" x2=\"116.0\" y2=\"70.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-3093)\"/><text x=\"122\" y=\"74\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">d</text><line x1=\"130.0\" y1=\"30.0\" x2=\"144.0\" y2=\"30.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-3093)\"/><rect x=\"144\" y=\"22\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"154\" y=\"33\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\u21912</text><line x1=\"164.0\" y1=\"30.0\" x2=\"176.0\" y2=\"30.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-3093)\"/><rect x=\"176\" y=\"22\" width=\"24\" height=\"16\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"188\" y=\"33\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">g\u2080</text><line x1=\"130.0\" y1=\"70.0\" x2=\"144.0\" y2=\"70.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-3093)\"/><rect x=\"144\" y=\"62\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"154\" y=\"73\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\u21912</text><line x1=\"164.0\" y1=\"70.0\" x2=\"176.0\" y2=\"70.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-3093)\"/><rect x=\"176\" y=\"62\" width=\"24\" height=\"16\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"188\" y=\"73\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">g\u2081</text><line x1=\"200.0\" y1=\"30.0\" x2=\"214.0\" y2=\"48.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-3093)\"/><line x1=\"200.0\" y1=\"70.0\" x2=\"214.0\" y2=\"52.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-3093)\"/><text x=\"224\" y=\"54\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">x\u0302</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">Haar: a[n] = (x[2n] + x[2n+1])/\u221a2</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">d[n] = (x[2n] \u2212 x[2n+1])/\u221a2</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"126\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">G\u2080H\u2080 + G\u2081H\u2081 = 2 ,  aliases cancel \u21d2 x\u0302 = x</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "The input x splits into approximation a (low-pass h\u2080, keep every second sample) and detail d (high-pass h\u2081). Upsampling and g\u2080, g\u2081 then rebuild x\u0302 = x.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Analysis:</strong> a low-pass $h_0$ gives the <strong>approximation</strong>, a high-pass $h_1$ gives the <strong>detail</strong>, each then <strong>downsampled by 2</strong>, so the total sample count is unchanged.",
      "<strong>Synthesis:</strong> upsample by 2 and filter with $g_0,g_1$, then add. <strong>Perfect reconstruction</strong> needs alias cancellation and no distortion: $G_0H_0+G_1H_1=2$ and $G_0(z)H_0(-z)+G_1(z)H_1(-z)=0$.",
      "<strong>Haar</strong> is the simplest bank: low-pass = pairwise average, high-pass = pairwise difference (scaled by $1/\\sqrt2$)."
    ],
    "math": "$$a[n]=\\frac{x[2n]+x[2n+1]}{\\sqrt2},\\quad d[n]=\\frac{x[2n]-x[2n+1]}{\\sqrt2},\\quad \\text{iterate on } a\\ \\text{for more levels}$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Splitting a row of the street frame in two.</strong> Take neighbouring pixels in pairs: their average goes into a half-size thumbnail row, their difference into a detail row. Nothing is lost because the pair can be rebuilt from the two numbers.",
    "examTrap": "Each channel is downsampled, so the high-pass band folds (aliases) in the spectrum. PR needs the synthesis filters to cancel that exactly.",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>Two-channel perfect-reconstruction filter bank.</b> The analysis bank filters $x$ with a low-pass $h_0$ and a high-pass $h_1$ and downsamples each by 2; the synthesis bank upsamples by 2, filters with $g_0,g_1$ and adds. The output equals the input (up to delay) if and only if the aliasing term cancels, $G_0(z)H_0(-z)+G_1(z)H_1(-z)=0$, and the distortion term is a pure delay, $G_0(z)H_0(z)+G_1(z)H_1(z)=2z^{-l}$. The Haar bank is $a[n]=\\frac{x[2n]+x[2n+1]}{\\sqrt2}$, $d[n]=\\frac{x[2n]-x[2n+1]}{\\sqrt2}$.",
    "hint": "After keeping half the samples in each channel, how can you still rebuild every pixel?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$h_0$ then $\\downarrow2$ = the coarse half.</strong> A low-pass keeps the smooth part, and halving the samples makes it a half-size picture.",
      "<strong>$h_1$ then $\\downarrow2$ = the detail half.</strong> A high-pass keeps the edges; together the two halves have as many samples as the original.",
      "<strong>Haar: average and difference.</strong> $(x_{2n}+x_{2n+1})/\\sqrt2$ and $(x_{2n}-x_{2n+1})/\\sqrt2$. The synthesis filters are chosen so the aliasing from the downsampling cancels exactly."
    ],
