    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-3101\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><text x=\"34\" y=\"12\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">f</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"18\" width=\"40\" height=\"20\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"34.0\" y=\"31.0\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">AB 12</text><text x=\"34\" y=\"50\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">true plate</text><line x1=\"58.0\" y1=\"28.0\" x2=\"82.0\" y2=\"28.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-3101)\"/><rect x=\"82\" y=\"16\" width=\"40\" height=\"24\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"102\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">h \u2217</text><text x=\"102\" y=\"35\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">motion</text><line x1=\"122.0\" y1=\"28.0\" x2=\"140.0\" y2=\"28.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-3101)\"/><text x=\"148\" y=\"32\" font-size=\"10\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">+</text><line x1=\"148.0\" y1=\"14.0\" x2=\"148.0\" y2=\"22.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-3101)\"/><text x=\"148\" y=\"10\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03b7</text><line x1=\"156.0\" y1=\"28.0\" x2=\"174.0\" y2=\"28.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-3101)\"/><text x=\"198\" y=\"12\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">g</text><rect x=\"178\" y=\"18\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#d9dee7\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"199\" y=\"31\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">A B 1 2</text><text x=\"199\" y=\"50\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">what the camera saw</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"82\" font-size=\"8.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">g = h \u2217 f + \u03b7   \u27f7   G = H F + N</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"98\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">noise is added after the blur: it is not blurred</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"114\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">restoration: model the damage, then estimate F\u0302 = W G</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "The true plate f is blurred by h (the car moving) and then speckle \u03b7 is added, giving the recorded frame g = h \u2217 f + \u03b7, or G = H F + N in frequency.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "The observed image is the true image <strong>blurred</strong> by the system $h$ (point-spread function) and then <strong>corrupted by additive noise</strong> $\\eta$.",
      "In frequency: <strong>$G(u,v)=H(u,v)F(u,v)+N(u,v)$</strong>, so deblurring is a per-frequency division problem that must also handle $N$.",
      "<strong>Restoration</strong> uses a model of the degradation (unlike enhancement, which is subjective) to build an estimate $\\hat F=W\\,G$."
    ],
    "math": "$$g(x,y)=(h\\ast f)(x,y)+\\eta(x,y)\\ \\ \\longleftrightarrow\\ \\ G(u,v)=H(u,v)F(u,v)+N(u,v)$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>The blurred number plate.</strong> A car drives past the pole camera during the exposure: the plate is smeared sideways (the $h$), and the night sensor adds speckle on top (the $\\eta$). Reading the plate means undoing the first without amplifying the second.",
    "examTrap": "Noise is added AFTER the blur, so it is not blurred. This is exactly why plain inversion by H blows the noise up.",
    "stmtKind": "DEFINITION",
    "statement": "<b>Image degradation model.</b> The observed image is $g(x,y)=(h\\ast f)(x,y)+\\eta(x,y)$, where $f$ is the true image, $h$ the point spread function of a linear shift-invariant degradation and $\\eta$ additive noise. In the frequency domain $G(u,v)=H(u,v)F(u,v)+N(u,v)$. Restoration seeks an estimate $\\hat F=W\\,G$ of $F$ using a model of $h$ and $\\eta$.",
    "hint": "When a moving car's plate is blurred by the camera, where in the formula is the noise added?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$h\\ast f$ = the blur.</strong> What the exposure does to the true plate: each point is smeared by the point spread function.",
      "<strong>$+\\,\\eta$ = noise added afterwards.</strong> Sensor noise lands on the already-blurred frame, so it is not blurred itself.",
      "<strong>$G=HF+N$ = the same in frequency.</strong> The convolution turns into a product, so each frequency of the plate is multiplied by $H(u,v)$ and noise is added; restoration has to undo $H$ without boosting $N$."
    ],
