    "highlighterClass": "highlight-amber",
    "title": "Inverse Filtering: Noise Blow-Up",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-3102\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"16.0\" y1=\"100.0\" x2=\"150.0\" y2=\"100.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-3102)\"/><line x1=\"16.0\" y1=\"100.0\" x2=\"16.0\" y2=\"14.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-3102)\"/><text x=\"150\" y=\"110\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">u</text><path d=\"M16.0,30.0 L18.5,30.2 L21.0,30.7 L23.4,31.5 L25.9,32.7 L28.4,34.2 L30.9,35.9 L33.4,37.9 L35.8,40.2 L38.3,42.6 L40.8,45.3 L43.3,48.0 L45.8,50.9 L48.2,53.8 L50.7,56.8 L53.2,59.8 L55.7,62.7 L58.2,65.6 L60.6,68.5 L63.1,71.2 L65.6,73.8 L68.1,76.3 L70.6,78.7 L73.0,80.9 L75.5,83.0 L78.0,85.0 L80.5,86.7 L83.0,88.4 L85.4,89.8 L87.9,91.2 L90.4,92.4 L92.9,93.4 L95.4,94.4 L97.8,95.2 L100.3,95.9 L102.8,96.6 L105.3,97.1 L107.8,97.6 L110.2,98.0 L112.7,98.3 L115.2,98.6 L117.7,98.9 L120.2,99.1 L122.6,99.3 L125.1,99.4 L127.6,99.5 L130.1,99.6 L132.6,99.7 L135.0,99.8 L137.5,99.8 L140.0,99.9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"86\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">|H|</text><path d=\"M16.0,91.0 L18.5,91.0 L21.0,90.9 L23.4,90.8 L25.9,90.6 L28.4,90.4 L30.9,90.2 L33.4,89.8 L35.8,89.5 L38.3,89.0 L40.8,88.5 L43.3,87.9 L45.8,87.2 L48.2,86.4 L50.7,85.4 L53.2,84.3 L55.7,83.1 L58.2,81.7 L60.6,80.0 L63.1,78.1 L65.6,75.9 L68.1,73.4 L70.6,70.4 L73.0,66.9 L75.5,62.9 L78.0,58.1 L80.5,52.5 L83.0,45.9 L85.4,38.1 L87.9,28.7 L90.4,17.6 L92.9,14.0 L95.4,14.0 L97.8,14.0 L100.3,14.0 L102.8,14.0 L105.3,14.0 L107.8,14.0 L110.2,14.0 L112.7,14.0 L115.2,14.0 L117.7,14.0 L120.2,14.0 L122.6,14.0 L125.1,14.0 L127.6,14.0 L130.1,14.0 L132.6,14.0 L135.0,14.0 L137.5,14.0 L140.0,14.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 2\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">1/|H|</text><rect x=\"104\" y=\"20\" width=\"40\" height=\"82\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.6\" stroke-dasharray=\"1 3\"/><text x=\"124\" y=\"118\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">noise zone</text><rect x=\"160\" y=\"20\" width=\"70\" height=\"62\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"195\" y=\"34\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">F\u0302 = G / H</text><text x=\"195\" y=\"48\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">= F + N / H</text><text x=\"195\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">H \u2192 0 \u21d2 N/H blows up</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"138\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">the plate turns to snow</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "The blur |H| falls toward 0 at high u. The inverse 1/|H| (dashed) shoots up there, multiplying the noise: F\u0302 = G/H = F + N/H.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Naive inverse:</strong> $\\hat F=G/H=F+N/H$, so with no noise it recovers $F$ exactly.",
      "<strong>Problem:</strong> real systems have $H\\to0$ at high frequencies (and sometimes exact zeros), so the error term <strong>$N/H$ is hugely amplified</strong> there and swamps the picture.",
      "<strong>Fixes:</strong> limit the inverse to frequencies where $|H|$ is large (a pseudo-inverse with a radius cut-off) or use <strong>Wiener / regularized</strong> filters."
    ],
    "math": "$$\\hat F(u,v)=\\frac{G(u,v)}{H(u,v)}=F(u,v)+\\frac{N(u,v)}{H(u,v)}$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Sharpening the plate too hard.</strong> Undoing the blur frequency by frequency works until the blur has erased a frequency: there the camera only recorded speckle, and dividing by almost zero multiplies that speckle until it covers the plate.",
    "examTrap": "If H(u,v) = 0 exactly the inverse is undefined (not just large). The 'N/H' term is the reason inverse filtering fails in noise.",
    "stmtKind": "PROPOSITION",
    "statement": "<b>Inverse filtering.</b> Given $G=HF+N$, the inverse filter estimate is $\\hat F(u,v)=\\dfrac{G(u,v)}{H(u,v)}=F(u,v)+\\dfrac{N(u,v)}{H(u,v)}$. Where $H(u,v)\\to0$ (typically at high frequencies, and exactly zero for some blurs) the term $N/H$ is arbitrarily large, so the estimate is dominated by amplified noise. The remedy is to restrict the division to frequencies where $|H|$ is large, or to use Wiener or regularized filters.",
    "hint": "Why does dividing by the blur give back the plate when there is no noise, and snow when there is?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$G/H=F+N/H$ = the right answer plus an error.</strong> With no noise the division cancels $H$ exactly and gives $F$ back.",
      "<strong>$H\\to0$ at high frequencies = the blur has wiped them out.</strong> Fine detail was nearly erased by the blur, so $|H|$ is tiny there.",
      "<strong>$N/H$ = noise divided by something tiny.</strong> The tiny numbers are exactly where only noise is left, and dividing by them makes it huge: the plate drowns in snow."
    ],
    "textbookImg": null,
    "textbookRef": null
