    "highlighterClass": "highlight-emerald",
    "title": "Wiener Filter: Don't Divide by Noise",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-3103\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"16.0\" y1=\"100.0\" x2=\"150.0\" y2=\"100.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-3103)\"/><line x1=\"16.0\" y1=\"100.0\" x2=\"16.0\" y2=\"14.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-3103)\"/><text x=\"150\" y=\"110\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">u</text><path d=\"M16.0,94.0 L18.5,94.0 L21.0,93.9 L23.4,93.9 L25.9,93.8 L28.4,93.6 L30.9,93.4 L33.4,93.2 L35.8,93.0 L38.3,92.7 L40.8,92.3 L43.3,91.9 L45.8,91.4 L48.2,90.9 L50.7,90.3 L53.2,89.6 L55.7,88.7 L58.2,87.8 L60.6,86.7 L63.1,85.4 L65.6,83.9 L68.1,82.2 L70.6,80.3 L73.0,78.0 L75.5,75.3 L78.0,72.1 L80.5,68.3 L83.0,63.9 L85.4,58.7 L87.9,52.5 L90.4,45.1 L92.9,36.2 L95.4,25.5 L97.8,14.0 L100.3,14.0 L102.8,14.0 L105.3,14.0 L107.8,14.0 L110.2,14.0 L112.7,14.0 L115.2,14.0 L117.7,14.0 L120.2,14.0 L122.6,14.0 L125.1,14.0 L127.6,14.0 L130.1,14.0 L132.6,14.0 L135.0,14.0 L137.5,14.0 L140.0,14.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 2\"/><text x=\"30\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">1/H</text><path d=\"M16.0,88.6 L18.5,88.5 L21.0,88.5 L23.4,88.3 L25.9,88.2 L28.4,87.9 L30.9,87.6 L33.4,87.3 L35.8,86.9 L38.3,86.4 L40.8,85.8 L43.3,85.2 L45.8,84.5 L48.2,83.7 L50.7,82.8 L53.2,81.9 L55.7,80.8 L58.2,79.8 L60.6,78.6 L63.1,77.5 L65.6,76.4 L68.1,75.3 L70.6,74.4 L73.0,73.7 L75.5,73.3 L78.0,73.2 L80.5,73.5 L83.0,74.3 L85.4,75.5 L87.9,77.0 L90.4,78.8 L92.9,80.8 L95.4,82.9 L97.8,84.9 L100.3,86.9 L102.8,88.8 L105.3,90.4 L107.8,91.9 L110.2,93.2 L112.7,94.4 L115.2,95.4 L117.7,96.2 L120.2,96.9 L122.6,97.5 L125.1,98.0 L127.6,98.4 L130.1,98.7 L132.6,99.0 L135.0,99.2 L137.5,99.3 L140.0,99.5\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"110\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">Wiener W</text><rect x=\"160\" y=\"20\" width=\"70\" height=\"76\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"195\" y=\"32\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">W =</text><text x=\"195\" y=\"46\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">H*</text><line x1=\"176\" y1=\"50\" x2=\"214\" y2=\"50\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/><text x=\"195\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">|H|\u00b2 + S\u03b7/Sf</text><text x=\"195\" y=\"82\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">F\u0302 = W G</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">strong |H|: W \u2248 1/H</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"137\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">weak |H|: W backs off, noise stays quiet</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "The inverse 1/H (dashed) explodes at high u. The Wiener filter W = H*/(|H|\u00b2 + S\u03b7/Sf) follows it where |H| is large and bends down where |H| is small.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Goal:</strong> choose $W$ to minimize the mean-squared error $E\\|f-\\hat f\\|^2$ given the noise-to-signal power ratio $S_\\eta/S_f$.",
      "<strong>Result:</strong> $W=\\dfrac{H^{*}}{|H|^{2}+S_\\eta/S_f}$. Where $|H|^{2}\\gg S_\\eta/S_f$ it acts like <strong>$1/H$</strong>; where $|H|$ is tiny it <strong>suppresses</strong> instead of exploding.",
      "<strong>Practical form:</strong> replace $S_\\eta/S_f$ by a constant $K$ tuned by eye. $K=0$ gives the inverse filter; larger $K$ gives smoother, blurrier output."
    ],
    "math": "$$W(u,v)=\\frac{H^{*}(u,v)}{|H(u,v)|^{2}+\\dfrac{S_\\eta(u,v)}{S_f(u,v)}},\\qquad \\hat F=W\\,G$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Know when the camera has no information.</strong> The Wiener filter sharpens the plate's strokes where the sensor recorded them clearly, and simply stays quiet at the frequencies the blur has buried in speckle.",
    "examTrap": "Wiener assumes known power spectra of signal and noise. Using the wrong K gives either ringing/noise (K too small) or over-blur (K too large).",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>Wiener filter.</b> For $g=h\\ast f+\\eta$ with $f,\\eta$ uncorrelated wide-sense stationary with power spectra $S_f,S_\\eta$, the linear filter minimizing $E\\|f-\\hat f\\|^2$ is $W(u,v)=\\dfrac{H^*(u,v)}{|H(u,v)|^2+S_\\eta(u,v)/S_f(u,v)}$, with $\\hat F=W\\,G$. In practice $S_\\eta/S_f$ is replaced by a constant $K$ chosen by eye: $K=0$ gives the inverse filter.",
    "hint": "How should a restoring filter act where the blur has nearly erased the plate's frequencies?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$H^*/|H|^2$ = the inverse where the signal is strong.</strong> When $|H|^2$ is much larger than the noise ratio, $W\\approx1/H$ and the blur is undone.",
      "<strong>$S_\\eta/S_f$ in the denominator = a safety margin.</strong> Where $|H|$ is tiny, the margin dominates and $W$ shrinks towards zero instead of exploding.",
      "<strong>$K$ = one knob by eye.</strong> $K=0$ is the inverse filter (snow); a larger $K$ gives a calmer but blurrier plate."
    ],
