    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-3104\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"18.0\" y1=\"106.0\" x2=\"130.0\" y2=\"106.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-3104)\"/><line x1=\"18.0\" y1=\"106.0\" x2=\"18.0\" y2=\"14.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-3104)\"/><text x=\"130\" y=\"116\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">\u2016g \u2212 Hf\u2016\u00b2 (misfit)</text><text x=\"14\" y=\"14\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">\u2016Pf\u2016\u00b2 (roughness)</text><path d=\"M22.0,34.8 L24.1,38.6 L26.2,42.6 L28.2,46.6 L30.3,50.4 L32.4,54.1 L34.5,57.6 L36.6,60.8 L38.6,63.7 L40.7,66.4 L42.8,68.9 L44.9,71.2 L47.0,73.3 L49.0,75.2 L51.1,77.0 L53.2,78.6 L55.3,80.1 L57.4,81.5 L59.4,82.8 L61.5,83.9 L63.6,85.0 L65.7,86.0 L67.8,86.9 L69.8,87.8 L71.9,88.6 L74.0,89.3 L76.1,90.0 L78.2,90.7 L80.2,91.3 L82.3,91.9 L84.4,92.4 L86.5,92.9 L88.6,93.4 L90.6,93.9 L92.7,94.3 L94.8,94.7 L96.9,95.1 L99.0,95.4 L101.0,95.8 L103.1,96.1 L105.2,96.4 L107.3,96.7 L109.4,97.0 L111.4,97.2 L113.5,97.5 L115.6,97.7 L117.7,98.0 L119.8,98.2 L121.8,98.4 L123.9,98.6 L126.0,98.8\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><circle cx=\"62.0\" cy=\"66.0\" r=\"2.4\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"66\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03b3 chosen here (corner)</text><rect x=\"150\" y=\"20\" width=\"80\" height=\"70\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"190\" y=\"33\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">min \u2016Pf\u2016\u00b2</text><text x=\"190\" y=\"45\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">s.t. \u2016g \u2212 Hf\u2016\u00b2 = \u2016\u03b7\u2016\u00b2</text><text x=\"190\" y=\"60\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">F\u0302 = H* G /</text><text x=\"190\" y=\"72\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">(|H|\u00b2 + \u03b3|P|\u00b2)</text><text x=\"190\" y=\"84\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">P = Laplacian</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"134\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">no power spectra needed: only the noise size</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "The L-curve plots roughness \u2016Pf\u2016\u00b2 against misfit \u2016g \u2212 Hf\u2016\u00b2; \u03b3 is chosen at the corner, where the restored plate fits the frame to within the noise \u2016\u03b7\u2016\u00b2.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Idea:</strong> minimize a <strong>smoothness measure</strong> $\\|Pf\\|^2$ (with $P$ a Laplacian) subject to the data constraint $\\|g-Hf\\|^2=\\|\\eta\\|^2$, which does not need the power spectra.",
      "<strong>Solution:</strong> $\\hat F=\\dfrac{H^{*}}{|H|^{2}+\\gamma|P|^{2}}G$, which looks just like Wiener but with a <strong>smoothness penalty weight $\\gamma$</strong>.",
      "<strong>Choose $\\gamma$</strong> by iterating until $\\|g-H\\hat f\\|^2\\approx\\|\\eta\\|^2$, or at the corner of the <strong>L-curve</strong> (misfit vs. smoothness)."
    ],
    "math": "$$\\min_f\\ \\|Pf\\|^2\\ \\text{s.t.}\\ \\|g-Hf\\|^2=\\|\\eta\\|^2\\ \\Rightarrow\\ \\hat F=\\frac{H^{*}}{|H|^{2}+\\gamma\\,|P(u,v)|^{2}}\\,G$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Smoothest plate that explains the footage.</strong> Of all the sharp-looking plates that blur into the recorded frame, pick the least jagged one, and accept a fit no better than the noise allows.",
    "examTrap": "Tikhonov/CLS and Wiener coincide only when \u03b3|P|\u00b2 equals S_\u03b7/S_f. In general they are different recipes with different knobs.",
    "stmtKind": "ALGORITHM",
    "statement": "<b>Constrained least-squares (CLS) restoration.</b> Minimize the roughness $\\|Pf\\|^2$ ($P$ the Laplacian operator) subject to $\\|g-Hf\\|^2=\\|\\eta\\|^2$. The solution in the frequency domain is $\\hat F(u,v)=\\dfrac{H^*(u,v)}{|H(u,v)|^2+\\gamma\\,|P(u,v)|^2}\\,G(u,v)$, where the Lagrange parameter $\\gamma$ is adjusted iteratively until $\\|g-H\\hat f\\|^2\\approx\\|\\eta\\|^2$ (or chosen at the corner of the L-curve).",
    "hint": "If you do not know the signal's power spectrum, what can you ask the restored plate to be instead?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$\\|Pf\\|^2$ = how rough the plate estimate is.</strong> The Laplacian $P$ is large on jagged edges and noise, so a small value means a smooth estimate.",
      "<strong>$\\|g-Hf\\|^2=\\|\\eta\\|^2$ = it must explain the frame up to the noise.</strong> Re-blurring the estimate must give back the recorded frame to within the size of the noise, only knowing $\\|\\eta\\|^2$.",
      "<strong>$\\gamma|P|^2$ = the smoothness price.</strong> Like Wiener's $K$, but weighted more at high frequencies; $\\gamma$ is tuned until the fit equals the noise level."
    ],
